--- !u!114 &395
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 62}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\n<size=70>So you're wondering how to play this entirely new puzzle element
    to Class of '09?\n<size=80>READ THIS TO LEARN\n\n\n<size=60>Core Controls\n<size=32>SWAP
    or ALT-SWAP will swap the blocks inside your cursor. There is only horizontal
    swapping.\nDirectional Inputs will move your cursor around.\nRAISE BLOCKS will
    raise your blocks from the bottom if you're low on blocks to solve with.\n\n\n<size=60>The
    Basics\n<size=40>The primary core of the game is lining up blocks of the same
    color in lines of 3 or more. These lines may be vertical or horizontal, whichever
    you find the quickest. Once you do that the blocks will pop away to clear room
    in your puzzle pod. These blocks will rise from the bottom at random and don't
    stop. This is not a shitty mobile match-3 game for your grandma, it requires
    SPEED. If you suck at clearing away these blocks quickly and one hits the top
    of your pod YOU LOSE.\n\n\n<size=60>Versus Puzzles\n<size=40>Most puzzle games
    are solo experiences, but not this one. This is a high speed puzzle figther against
    the CPU or second player. Instead of throwing punches you throw garbage blocks
    on top of your opponent's current stack. If one of these hits the top of your
    pod you still lose. Combos of 4 or higher send garbage blocks but chains with
    high multiples throw garbage mountains! Garbage blocks contain additional blocks
    within for you to use and must be unlocked by getting a clear that is bordering
    said garbage block. You will want to prioritize high combos and chains to bury
    your opponent in garbage!\n\n\n<size=60>Chaining\n<size=40>While clearing 3 blocks
    at once is cool, chains are the most important strat you need to learn! While
    a standard clear is popping the blocks away you will notice that the blocks that
    were above them were hovering for a short amount of time. If those blocks which
    were on top of the hovering area fall into another solve it creates a 2x chain.
    If blocks above that 2x chain fall into ANOTHER solve it will create a 3x chain,
    and so on and so forth. It is important to learn how to manipulate the blocks
    around hovering areas post-clear to maximize the amount of chains you're doing.
    Requires very quick fingers! If you do not become experienced in this you will
    not do well at this game. To repeat: <size=54>If you do not learn how to chain
    consistently you will be trash at this game.<size=40> This will require a lot
    of practice, but once you learn you will have far less trouble beating more advanced
    opponents.\n\n      ."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: de0cf02bc81842a45a93520a6824d71a, type: 2}
